    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.extra, mini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI prefer my previews to center the line instead of the default top position, so I have this in my config:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  require(\"mini.pick\").setup({\r\n    source = {\r\n      preview = function(buf_id, item)\r\n        return MiniPick.default_preview(buf_id, item, { line_position = \"center\" })\r\n      end\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works for pickers defined in 'mini.pick' (grep for example), but it does not seem to apply to the pickers defined in 'mini.extra' (buf_lines for example). What would be the recommended way of setting the default options for `MiniPick.default_preview` for pickers defined in 'mini.extra'?\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\np.s. And, out of curiosity, why is top the default? I prefer to have context both before and afterwards when previewing. And I'm legitimately surprised that someone would not, but I'm probably not thinking of some use case that I just don't use.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.extra, mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I prefer my previews to center the line instead of the default top position, so I have this in my config:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  require(&quot;mini.pick&quot;).setup({\n    source = {\n      preview = function(buf_id, item)\n        return MiniPick.default_preview(buf_id, item, { line_position = &quot;center&quot; })\n      end\n    }\n  })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">  <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">source</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-en\">preview</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">buf_id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">default_preview</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">buf_id</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">item</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">line_position</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>center<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n    }\n  })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This works for pickers defined in 'mini.pick' (grep for example), but it does not seem to apply to the pickers defined in 'mini.extra' (buf_lines for example). What would be the recommended way of setting the default options for <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniPick.default_preview</code> for pickers defined in 'mini.extra'?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">p.s. And, out of curiosity, why is top the default? I prefer to have context both before and afterwards when previewing. And I'm legitimately surprised that someone would not, but I'm probably not thinking of some use case that I just don't use.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.extra, mini.pick\nQuestion\nI prefer my previews to center the line instead of the default top position, so I have this in my config:\n  require(\"mini.pick\").setup({\n    source = {\n      preview = function(buf_id, item)\n        return MiniPick.default_preview(buf_id, item, { line_position = \"center\" })\n      end\n    }\n  })\nThis works for pickers defined in 'mini.pick' (grep for example), but it does not seem to apply to the pickers defined in 'mini.extra' (buf_lines for example). What would be the recommended way of setting the default options for MiniPick.default_preview for pickers defined in 'mini.extra'?\nThanks!\np.s. And, out of curiosity, why is top the default? I prefer to have context both before and afterwards when previewing. And I'm legitimately surprised that someone would not, but I'm probably not thinking of some use case that I just don't use.",
